---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import SectionMarker from '../components/SectionMarker.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { links } from '../lib/site';

const publishers = ['PedalPCB', 'GuitarPCB', 'Aion FX', 'Five Cats', 'Tonepad'];
---

<Base description="Star Ground turns guitar pedal build documents into one shopping list: it merges their parts lists, subtracts what you own, and flags anything it may have misread.">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">FOR DIY GUITAR PEDAL BUILDERS</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">One shopping list for every pedal you're building.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Give Star Ground the build documents for your next pedals. It reads each parts list, merges
        them, subtracts the parts you already own, and tells you exactly what to check wherever it
        isn't sure it read the document right.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="hs-button hs-button--primary" href={links.app}>
          Try the current app <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} />
        </a>
        <a class="hs-button" href={links.github}>
          <Icon name="brand-github" size={16} /> View the source
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">
        The app is being rebuilt here. Until then, the current version does the same work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="sections">
    <section id="how-it-works" class="section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionMarker number={1} label="How it works" />
        <h2 id="how-title">From a stack of build documents to one parts order.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Each pedal's build document lists its parts. Copying those lists by hand is slow, and one
          missed resistor stalls a build for weeks. Star Ground does the copying and shows its work.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <h3>Add your builds</h3>
            <p>
              Upload a build document, paste a link to one, pick a circuit from the preset library,
              or paste a parts list as lines like <code>R1 10k</code>.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Check what it read</h3>
            <p>
              Self-checks read each document again independently. Wherever the parts list could
              disagree with the document, you get a warning that names the part to check.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Buy and build</h3>
            <p>
              Get one shopping list across every project, net of your stock and with spares where
              running out would stall you, plus supplier cart files, build checklists, and bin
              labels.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="documents" class="section" aria-labelledby="documents-title">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionMarker number={2} label="Documents" />
        <h2 id="documents-title">Reads the build documents of five PCB publishers.</h2>
        <ul class="publishers" aria-label="Supported publishers">
          {publishers.map((name) => (
            <li>{name}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="section-lead">
          It handles ruled tables, side-by-side lists, and documents that describe several circuits,
          where you choose the one you're building. Parts lists printed as images are read by OCR
          only if you ask, and every part OCR read is listed for you to check. Other publishers'
          documents aren't tested, so expect more warnings there, or parts it can't read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="accuracy" class="section" aria-labelledby="accuracy-title">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionMarker number={3} label="Accuracy" />
        <h2 id="accuracy-title">Graded against parts lists checked by hand.</h2>
        <dl class="facts">
          <div>
            <dt>1,240</dt>
            <dd>Build documents labeled</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>60,000</dt>
            <dd>Parts checked by hand</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>0</dt>
            <dd>Silent errors on those documents</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="section-lead">
          The parser reads each page's word positions and table lines, with no language model, so a
          document always gives the same list. It can still be wrong, but not silently: on every
          labeled document, each wrong or missing part carries a warning. New documents can differ
          from the labeled ones, so check the warnings it shows you.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${links.github}#readme`}>
          How it's measured <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={14} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
